+### Local Provider Setup (UI)
+
+You do not need a Grok account to use a local model. On the login screen, press `s` (**Skip login (use a local model)**). In a session, run `/local-provider`. Either one opens a setup form:
+
+| Field | Notes |
+|-------|-------|
+| Provider | `←`/`→` cycles Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp server, vLLM, and Custom; each one fills in its default base URL |
+| Base URL | OpenAI-compatible root, e.g. `http://localhost:11434/v1` |
+| Model | Detected from `{base_url}/models` when the form opens or the URL changes (`Ctrl+R` re-detects, `Ctrl+N`/`Ctrl+P` cycles) |
+| API key | Optional. Local servers ignore it; when you leave it blank, the placeholder `local` is written |
+| Context window | Optional. Defaults to 200,000 tokens |
+
+`Enter` saves the model as a `[model.<provider>-<model>]` entry in `~/.grok/config.toml` and sets it as `[models] default`. If `[models] session_summary` is unset, it is pinned to the same model, so session titles don't go to a Grok model the local server doesn't have. The file is written owner-only (`0600`). Because the entry has its own `api_key`, Grok authenticates without an xAI login, and later launches skip the login screen. If a local model is already configured, `s` on the login screen signs in with it immediately.
+
+Built-in Grok models still need `grok login` or `XAI_API_KEY`.
+
